    dct:identifier "38" ;
    skos:definition "Information on relevant supply chain indices"@en ;
    skos:note "As a non-mandatory data attribute the battery passport should contain supply chain indices to allow easy assessment for consumers on level of responsible sourcing. ESGE+ indices under development by the GBA (Global Battery Alliance), scoring and benchmarking sustainability performance. Once developed, explore how to best make the indices available via the battery passport."@en ;
    dct:relation "DIN DKE Spec 99100 6.4.4" ;
    dpp:dataFormat "String" ;
    dpp:accessRights dpp:Public ;
    dpp:dataBehaviour dpp:Static ;
    dpp:granularityLevel dpp:BatteryModel ;
    dpp:granularityLevelDetail "Pack: x" ;
    dpp:applicableTo dpp:ElectricVehicleBattery, dpp:LightMeansOfTransportBattery, dpp:OtherIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh, dpp:StationaryIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh ;
    skos:example "Applicability — EV: o; LMT: o; Other Industrial >2kWh: o; Stationary >2kWh: o" .

dpp:batteryChemistry
    a owl:DatatypeProperty, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy dpp: ;
    rdfs:domain dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "Battery chemistry"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Battery chemistry"@en ;
    skos:inScheme dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    dct:identifier "39" ;
    skos:definition "The electrochemical composition reflecting active materials in cathode and anode, and - voluntarily - electrolyte"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """The battery passport must contain information on the battery chemistry of the battery.

The battery chemistry must also be provided on the battery label

Base on the labelling IA (currently available as draft), the following terms shall be used:

Lead acid: “Pb”
Nickel cadmium: “Ni-Cd”
Nickel metal hydride: “Ni-MH”
Lithium ion NMC: “Li-ion NMC”
Lithium ion LFP: “Li-ion LFP”
Lithium ion LMO: “Li-ion LMO”
Lithium ion LCO: “Li-ion LCO”
Lithium ion NCA: “Li-ion NCA”
Lithium metal: “Li-metal”
Sodium-ion: “Na-ion”

For secondary (rechargeable) batteries whose electrochemical composition does not correspond to any of the categories listed above, it shall be indicated based on the molecular formula of the cathode and/or anode."""@en ;
    skos:note "The battery chemistry should relate to the naming of the cathode, anode, and electrolyte of the battery."@en ;
    dpp:regulationReference "Annex XIII (1b); Annex VI Part A (7); Labelling IA (draft)" ;
    dct:relation "DIN DKE Spec 99100 6.5.2" ;
    dpp:dataFormat "String" ;
    dpp:accessRights dpp:Public ;
    dpp:dataBehaviour dpp:Static ;
    dpp:granularityLevel dpp:BatteryModel ;
    dpp:granularityLevelDetail "Pack: x" ;
    dpp:applicableTo dpp:ElectricVehicleBattery, dpp:LightMeansOfTransportBattery, dpp:OtherIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh, dpp:StationaryIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh ;
    skos:example "Applicability — EV: x; LMT: x; Other Industrial >2kWh: x; Stationary >2kWh: x" .

dpp:criticalRawMaterials
    a owl:DatatypeProperty, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy dpp: ;
    rdfs:domain dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "Critical raw materials"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Critical raw materials"@en ;
    skos:inScheme dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    dct:identifier "40" ;
    skos:definition "Critical raw materials present in a concentration of more than 0,1%, weight by weight"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """The battery passport must contain information on the critical raw materials present in the battery. Critical raw materials are listed in Annex II of Regulation (EU) 2024/1252.

The information on the critical raw materials must also be provided on the battery label.

Per Annex VI, Part A(10), critical raw materials must be reported if present in the battery in a concentration of more than 0,1 % weight by weight."""@en ;
    dpp:regulationReference "Annex XIII (1b); Annex VI Part A (10); Labelling IA (draft)" ;
    dct:relation "DIN DKE Spec 99100 6.5.3" ;
    dpp:dataFormat "String" ;
    dpp:accessRights dpp:Public ;
    dpp:dataBehaviour dpp:Static ;
    dpp:granularityLevel dpp:BatteryModel ;
    dpp:granularityLevelDetail "Pack: x" ;
    dpp:applicableTo dpp:ElectricVehicleBattery, dpp:LightMeansOfTransportBattery, dpp:OtherIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh, dpp:StationaryIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh ;
    skos:example "Applicability — EV: x; LMT: x; Other Industrial >2kWh: x; Stationary >2kWh: x" .

dpp:materialsUsedInCathodeAnodeAndElectrolyte
    a owl:DatatypeProperty, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy dpp: ;
    rdfs:domain dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "Materials used in cathode, anode and electrolyte"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Materials used in cathode, anode and electrolyte"@en ;
    skos:inScheme dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    dct:identifier "41" ;
    skos:definition "Detailed composition of cathode, anode and electrolyte"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """The battery passport must contain information on the detailed composition of the battery.

Information on the detailed composition must include materials used in the cathode, anode and electrolyte."""@en ;
    skos:note """Access to this information should be additionally, at least, provided to sorters, dismantlers, and recyclers.

A \"material\" should relate to the composition of its constituent chemical components in order to report on the detailed composition of a battery model by specifying the materials used in the entire battery.

Materials should be reported for the as-built battery.

Materials in the battery should be reported above a concentration of 1 % weight by weight. Thereby, the threshold of 1 % should be determined as the overall content of the material in the battery in relation to the mass of the entire battery, as defined per technical documentation referred to in Annex VIII.

The mass should be specified in terms of kg of a material in the entire battery, as defined per technical documentation referred to in BattReg Annex VIII.

The materials should be named using a public standard or agreed nomenclature, which refers e.g. to the nomenclature of IUPAC or related identifiers such as the CAS (Chemical Abstracts Service) number."""@en ;
    dpp:regulationReference "Annex XIII (2a)" ;
    dct:relation "DIN DKE Spec 99100 6.5.4" ;
    dpp:dataFormat "Array (string)" ;
    dpp:dataBehaviour dpp:Static ;
    dpp:granularityLevel dpp:BatteryModel ;
    dpp:granularityLevelDetail "Pack: x" ;
    dpp:applicableTo dpp:ElectricVehicleBattery, dpp:LightMeansOfTransportBattery, dpp:OtherIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh, dpp:StationaryIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh ;
    skos:example "Applicability — EV: x; LMT: x; Other Industrial >2kWh: x; Stationary >2kWh: x" .

dpp:hazardousSubstances
    a owl:DatatypeProperty, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy dpp: ;
    rdfs:domain dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "Hazardous substances"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hazardous substances"@en ;
    skos:inScheme dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    dct:identifier "42" ;
    skos:definition "Substances of very high concern in the meaning of Article 3 (1) (69) which are present in the battery, other than mercury, cadmium and lead, with a concentration equal or above 0,1%, weight on weight.’"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """The battery passport must contain information on substances of very high concern other than mercury, cadmium, or lead contained in the battery.

substances of very high concern in the meaning of Article 3 (1) (69) which are present in the battery, other than mercury, cadmium and lead, with a concentration equal or above 0,1%, weight on weight.
‘substance of very high concern’ means any substance which fulfils the criteria laid down in Article 57 of Regulation (EC) No 1907/2006 [REACH] and is identified in accordance with Article 59(1) of that Regulation, or any substance which fulfils the criteria laid down in Article 57 of Regulation (EC) No 1907/2006 [REACH] and listed in Annex VI of Regulation (EC) 1272/2008 [CLP Regulation].’

Substances of very high concern and those for which there is a restriction in BattReg Annex I [mercury, cadmium, lead] are required to be named in accordance with their nomenclature in Regulation (EC) 1272/2008 (\"CLP Regulation\").

The information on hazardous substances must also be provided on the battery label.

BattReg Article 74(3) states that the location of the hazardous substances in the battery must be identified. This requirement needs to be provided upon request even though it is not specifically for the battery passport and can be integrated."""@en ;
    skos:note """Substances should be reported on as chemical element and its compounds in the natural state or obtained by any manufacturing process, as per Regulations EC No 1907/2006 and EC No 1272/2008.

A nomenclature for hazardous substances should relate to the nomenclature of IUPAC, as required under Regulation EC No 1907/2006. Other identifiers such as the CAS (Chemical Abstracts Service) or EC number can be added if available.

The hazards of the substances should be specified.(see separate data attribute)

The mass of the hazardous substances should be reported for a battery model.
The mass can be reported in terms of kg of a material and in terms of the concentration of weight by weight % in the entire battery, as defined per technical documentation referred to in Annex VIII. The SCIP guidance for concentration ranges should be used."""@en ;
    dpp:regulationReference """Annex XIII (1b); Annex VI Part A (8); Labelling IA (draft),
Environmental Omnibus: Draft: 2025/0397 (COD), Art. 1 (4)""" ;
    dct:relation "DIN DKE Spec 99100 6.5.5" ;
    dpp:dataFormat "Array (string)" ;
    dpp:accessRights dpp:Public ;
    dpp:dataBehaviour dpp:Static ;
    dpp:granularityLevel dpp:BatteryModel ;
    dpp:granularityLevelDetail "Pack: x" ;
    dpp:applicableTo dpp:ElectricVehicleBattery, dpp:LightMeansOfTransportBattery, dpp:OtherIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh, dpp:StationaryIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh ;
    skos:example "Applicability — EV: x; LMT: x; Other Industrial >2kWh: x; Stationary >2kWh: x" .

dpp:impactOfSubstancesOnEnvironmentHumanHealthSafetyPersons
    a owl:DatatypeProperty, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy dpp: ;
    rdfs:domain dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "Impact of substances on environment, human health, safety, persons"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Impact of substances on environment, human health, safety, persons"@en ;
    skos:inScheme dpp:BatteryMaterialsAndComposition ;
    dct:identifier "43" ;
    skos:definition "Elaboration on the impact of substances contained in the battery on the environment, human health and the safety of persons"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The battery passport must contain information on the impact of substances, in particular hazardous substances, present in the battery. Hereby the impact on the environment and on human health or the safety of persons is considered and includes the impact due to inappropriate discarding of waste batteries, such as littering or discarding as unsorted municipal waste."@en ;
    skos:note """The classification for “hazardous substances” should be defined as per Regulation EC No 1272/2008 (“CLP Regulation”).

The impact should be described by using commonly used statements, which can be reported by hazard (H) phrases and precautionary (P) statements as per Regulation EC No 1272/2008 (“CLP Regulation”).

The impact should be reported as required per Regulation EC No 1907/2006 (“REACH Regulation”) registration obligations.

The impact of substances on environment, human health, safety, persons may also be included in the data attribute 'hazardous substances'"""@en ;
    dpp:regulationReference "Annex XIII (1s); Art. 74 1(f)" ;
    dct:relation "DIN DKE Spec 99100 6.5.6" ;
    dpp:dataFormat "String" ;
    dpp:accessRights dpp:Public ;
    dpp:dataBehaviour dpp:Static ;
    dpp:granularityLevel dpp:BatteryModel ;
    dpp:granularityLevelDetail "Pack: x" ;
    dpp:applicableTo dpp:ElectricVehicleBattery, dpp:LightMeansOfTransportBattery, dpp:OtherIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh, dpp:StationaryIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh ;
    skos:example "Applicability — EV: x; LMT: x; Other Industrial >2kWh: x; Stationary >2kWh: x" .

dpp:dismantlingInformationManualsForTheRemovalAndTheDisassemblyOfTheBatteryPack
    a owl:DatatypeProperty, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy dpp: ;
    rdfs:domain dpp:CircularityAndResourceEfficiency_CircularityInformation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:label "Dismantling information: Manuals for the removal and the disassembly of the battery pack"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dismantling information: Manuals for the removal and the disassembly of the battery pack"@en ;
    skos:inScheme dpp:CircularityAndResourceEfficiency ;
    dct:identifier "44" ;
    skos:definition "Manual(s) containing information on the removal and disassembly of the battery pack"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """A battery passport must include dismantling information.

The dismantling information must include:
- exploded diagrams of the battery system/pack showing the location of battery cells;
- disassembly sequences;
- type and number of fastening techniques to be unlocked;
- tools required for disassembly;
- warnings if risk of damaging parts exist; and
- amount of cells used and layout."""@en ;
    skos:note """The dismantling information required by the EU Battery Regulation should be integrated into two separate manuals, a manual for the removal of the battery pack and a manual for the disassembly of the battery pack.

The manual for the removal of the battery pack and the manual for disassembly of the battery pack should be machine-readable whenever possible.

The manual for the removal of the battery pack should include:
- information on whether it is possible to remove the battery from the appliance or not;
- removal sequences;
- characteristics of the joints, screws, and fasteners: type, number, materials and number of fastening techniques to be unlocked;
- electrical and electromechanical interfaces important for the removal from the appliance;
- tools required for battery removal;
- risk warnings and safety measures.

The manual for disassembly of the battery pack should include:
- information on whether it is possible to disassemble the battery pack;
If disassembly of the battery pack is possible, information on the re-assembly of the battery should also be provided.
- information on replaceability of modules and cells (replacement possible or not possible);
If replacement of modules and cells is possible, information on the replacement steps should be provided.
- exploded diagrams of the battery system/pack showing the location of the battery cells and modules, including format and dimensions of battery cells, modules and pack, and orientation of the battery cells;
- type of construction of battery pack, modules, and cells;
- disassembly sequences;
- characteristics of joints, screws, and fasteners: type, number, materials, and number of fastening techniques to be unlocked;
- electrical and electromechanical interfaces important for the disassembly and dismantling process;
- information on fillings, if used: characteristics of foams and/or glues;
- information on casing: type and material (steel/plastic);
- tools required for disassembly;
- risk warnings and safety measures."""@en ;
    dpp:regulationReference "Annex XIII (2c);" ;
    dct:relation "DIN DKE Spec 99100 6.6.1.2" ;
    dpp:dataFormat "URI/URL" ;
    dpp:dataBehaviour dpp:Static ;
    dpp:granularityLevel dpp:BatteryModel ;
    dpp:granularityLevelDetail "Pack: x" ;
    dpp:applicableTo dpp:ElectricVehicleBattery, dpp:LightMeansOfTransportBattery, dpp:OtherIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh, dpp:StationaryIndustrialBatteryAbove2kWh ;
    skos:example "Applicability — EV: x; LMT: x; Other Industrial >2kWh: x; Stationary >2kWh: x" .

